1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
 In days lecture we will understand Docker volumes and how to use them in Dockerize.net apps.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,800
 Volumes are persistent data stores for containers.

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:20,640
 Here you can keep your data so that it remains safe even if the container crashes.

4
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:27,520
 Volumes are stored within the directory of the Docker host which is our PC

5
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:36,560
 and so when we mount a volume into a container this directory is what's mounted into the container.

6
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:44,080
 The picture explains Docker volumes. Here is the container which is referencing a Docker volume.

7
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:51,840
 This volume contains important files for the apps and is stored outside the container on the

8
00:00:52,480 --> 00:01:00,480
 local PC where Docker desktop is installed. So this means the app files are safe even if the container

9
